UID:queer-art-illuminations-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T203645Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260702
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260703
SUMMARY:Deadline: Illuminations Grant for Black Trans Women Visual Artists
DESCRIPTION:Now in its 7th year\, the Illuminations Grant for Black Trans W
 omen Visual Artists is an annual USD 10\,000 grant from Queer|Art that pro
 vides critical support to Black trans women whose work has often been unde
 r-recognized in the visual art field. To further recognize finalists for t
 heir artistic achievements\, Queer|Art also provides a USD 1\,250 award to
  four distinguished finalists. Winning artists and finalists receive addit
 ional professional development resources and further guidance to bolster t
 heir creative development. The grant was developed and named in partnershi
 p with Mariette Pathy Allen\, Aaryn Lang\, and Serena Jara\, and is made p
 ossible entirely through support from visual artist Mariette Pathy Allen\,
  whose photographic work over the last forty years has focused on expandin
 g cultural consciousness around gender and transformation. It is administe
 red through Queer|Art with a rotating panel of judges\, each of whom condu
 cts a studio visit with the winning artist as part of the award's focus on
  creative and professional development\; judges for the 2026 cycle include
  Jordyn Jay\, Isis Awad\, and Utē Petit. ELIGIBILITY: qualified artists m
 ust be self-identified Black trans women and trans femmes working in visua
 l art and based in the United States. Deadline: July 2\, 2026.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Queer|Art\nLocation: United States\; open to self-identified Black t
 rans women and trans femmes working in visual art and based in the US.\nAw
 ard: USD 10\,000 to one winning artist\, plus USD 1\,250 each to four dist
 inguished finalists. Winners and finalists also receive additional profess
 ional development resources and guidance\, and each judge conducts a studi
 o visit with the winning artist.\nDuration: One-time award\n\nMore: https:
 //www.queer-art.org/illuminations-grant?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.queer-art.org/illuminations-grant?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United States\; open to self-identified Black trans women and tran
 s femmes working in visual art and based in the US.
END:VEVENT
