BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:community-engagement-artists-creatives-grant-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T203645Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: Artists and Creatives Grant\, Fall 2026
DESCRIPTION:Community Engagement\, a 501(c)(3) nonprofit based in Orange Co
 unty\, California\, funds independent creatives making or presenting work 
 that relates to or encourages community engagement. Its framing is collabo
 rative placemaking\, projects from communal gardens to public mosaics to i
 ntergenerational art activities that reimagine shared spaces and stimulate
  social engagement\, creative expression and collective empowerment\, with
  a focus on diverse and underserved neighbourhoods. GEOGRAPHY DEPENDS ON T
 HE ROUND: the fall round\, deadline 15 September\, is open only to artists
  living or working in California. The spring round\, deadline 15 March\, i
 s open to artists living or working anywhere in the US. WHAT IT FUNDS: the
  execution of community-engaged projects\, prioritising the creation of ne
 w artworks that present new and imaginative possibilities. The funder says
  it is not likely to fund art classes\, take-home art kits\, or exhibition
 s of studio artwork in preexisting galleries unless the proposal centres a
  clear and purposeful collaboration with a community. WHO CAN APPLY: indiv
 idual artists and artist collectives\, including collaborators. NOT SUPPOR
 TED: arts festivals\, nonprofit and for-profit organizations\, student pro
 jects (undergraduate or graduate)\, residencies\, research symposia\, stud
 io rent\, conferences\, theaters\, and any activity affiliated with religi
 ous organizations. Successful grantees must wait at least two years before
  reapplying. The grant explicitly encourages applications from artists his
 torically underrepresented in the arts\, including Black\, Indigenous\, Pe
 ople of Color\, Queer\, Trans\, Deaf\, Disabled\, Immigrant\, Refugee and 
 Self-Taught artists. HOW TO APPLY: upload four PDFs to a single publicly a
 ccessible online folder (Google Drive\, Dropbox or similar) and submit the
  link via the form\; documents not in PDF format will not be considered. A
 pplications that do not follow the guidelines are not reviewed\, and if yo
 u have not heard back six weeks after the deadline the application was uns
 uccessful. Deadline 15 September 2026 at 11:59pm PST\, with decisions 15 O
 ctober.\n\nOrganisation: Community Engagement\nLocation: California\, USA 
 for the fall round. The spring round (March deadline) is open to artists l
 iving or working anywhere in the US.\nAward: Usually USD 500 to USD 2\,500
 \, and in rare circumstances up to USD 5\,000. The funder suggests most ar
 tists apply for under USD 2\,500 unless advised otherwise. No application 
 fee.\nDuration: Project-based grant\n\nMore: https://www.communityengageme
 nt.org/how-to-apply?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.communityengagement.org/how-to-apply?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:California\, USA for the fall round. The spring round (March deadl
 ine) is open to artists living or working anywhere in the US.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:glean-portland-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T203645Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: GLEAN 2027 Call for Artists
DESCRIPTION:GLEAN\, meaning to collect gradually bit by bit\, is a juried a
 rt programme that taps the creativity of artists to make people think abou
 t their consumption habits\, the waste they generate and the resources the
 y throw away. Each year five local artists\, chosen by a jury of arts and 
 environmental professionals\, get access to the Metro Central transfer sta
 tion for five months to glean discarded materials and make work from them.
  The programme ends with a group exhibition of the results at a local gall
 ery in the summer. The 2027 round carries an increased stipend of USD 3\,0
 00 per artist and another collaboration with Rainmaker Craft Initiative. L
 aunched in 2010\, GLEAN is a partnership between Recology Oregon Recovery 
 Inc.\, an employee-owned company managing resource recovery facilities\, M
 etro\, the regional government running the Portland area's garbage and rec
 ycling system\, and ReClaim It\, a nonprofit environmental arts organizati
 on. ELIGIBILITY: artists from Portland\, Oregon. Applications are open 1 A
 ugust to 13 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: GLEAN (Recology Oregon Recove
 ry\, Metro and ReClaim It)\, with Rainmaker Craft Initiative\nLocation: Po
 rtland\, Oregon\, USA. Open to artists from Portland\; work takes place at
  the Metro Central transfer station.\nAward: Stipend of USD 3\,000 per art
 ist\, increased from previous years. Five local artists are selected. Arti
 sts also receive five months of access to the Metro Central transfer stati
 on to gather discarded materials\, and the programme culminates in a group
  exhibition at a local gallery. This round includes another collaboration 
 with Rainmaker Craft Initiative. No application fee is mentioned.\nDuratio
 n: Five months of access to the transfer station\, culminating in a summer
  exhibition\n\nMore: https://www.gleanportland.com/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.gleanportland.com/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Portland\, Oregon\, USA. Open to artists from Portland\; work take
 s place at the Metro Central transfer station.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vcca-anne-spencer-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T203645Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: VCCA Anne Spencer Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:Named fellowship at VCCA's Mt. San Angelo campus in rural Virgi
 nia\, established in 2017 in honour of Harlem Renaissance poet and civil r
 ights activist Anne Spencer. It funds a one-month residency plus a USD 1\,
 500 honorarium for writers\, visual artists and composers of African Ameri
 can descent. WHAT YOU GET: private bedroom with private bath\, a separate 
 individual studio away from the bedroom\, and three meals a day\, inside a
  cross-disciplinary community of resident artists\, so the entire cost of 
 being there is carried by VCCA and the honorarium is on top of it. THE ONE
  CATCH ON ELIGIBILITY THIS CYCLE: the fellowship is described as open to w
 riters\, visual artists and composers\, but the 2027 application details n
 arrow the current round to WRITERS\, with preference given to those of Afr
 ican American descent. Read that as a writing-focused cycle rather than an
  open call to all three disciplines. COMMUNITY COMMITMENT: Anne Spencer Fe
 llows tour the Anne Spencer House and Garden Museum in Lynchburg and take 
 part in one Lynchburg-community activity\, choosing between a public prese
 ntation\, a workshop at an Anne Spencer partner school\, or another commun
 ity-based activity coordinated with the Anne Spencer Memorial Foundation. 
 Budget time for this\; it is not optional. HOW TO APPLY: there is no stand
 alone form. Complete the 'Application for Mt. San Angelo Residencies\, VCC
 A in Virginia\, Summer 2027' and select your fellowship interest at Questi
 on 2. A USD 30 application fee applies. Residency dates are drawn from 1 M
 ay to 31 August 2027 and decisions land by 31 December 2026.\n\nOrganisati
 on: Virginia Center for the Creative Arts (VCCA)\nLocation: Mt. San Angelo
 \, Amherst\, Virginia\, United States\, with activities in the nearby Lync
 hburg community.\nAward: USD 1\,500 honorarium paid on completion of the r
 esidency\, on top of a fully funded one-month stay: a private bedroom with
  private bath\, a separate individual studio and three meals a day. Applic
 ation fee USD 30.\nDuration: One month\, scheduled inside the 1 May to 31 
 August 2027 window. Applications open 1 June 2026\, deadline 15 September 
 2026\, notification by 31 December 2026.\n\nMore: https://www.vcca.com/app
 ly/fully-funded-fellowships/anne-spencer-fellowship/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.vcca.com/apply/fully-funded-fellowships/anne-spencer-fellow
 ship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Mt. San Angelo\, Amherst\, Virginia\, United States\, with activit
 ies in the nearby Lynchburg community.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:frameline-completion-fund-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T203645Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261010
SUMMARY:Deadline: Frameline Completion Fund 2027
DESCRIPTION:Long-running post-production grant from Frameline\, the San Fra
 ncisco organisation behind the world's longest-running LGBTQ+ film festiva
 l\, for films that represent and reflect LGBTQ+ life in all its complexity
  and richness. Grants run up to USD 5\,000\, typically USD 1\,000 to 5\,00
 0\, and the jury may recommend more or less than that range. WHAT IT COVER
 S: any post-production cost\, explicitly including editing\, special effec
 ts and graphics\, music licensing\, photo licensing\, and\, notably\, clos
 ed captioning and audio description\, so accessibility work is fundable ra
 ther than an afterthought. STAGE GATE\, the thing that disqualifies most a
 pplicants: your project must be at least 90 percent complete with a rough 
 cut available\, and in or about to enter post-production. Work still in de
 velopment or mid-production is not eligible. WHO AND WHAT: all formats\, l
 engths\, genres and nationalities are welcome\, spanning documentary\, nar
 rative\, experimental\, animated and episodic work\, so long as the film i
 s about LGBTQ+ people and their communities. Directors must have creative 
 and financial control of the project. NO APPLICATION FEE\, which is worth 
 flagging given how many completion funds charge one. TIMING: the submissio
 n window opens 31 August 2026 and closes 9 October 2026\, with decisions i
 n January 2027. The 2026 cycle's grantees have already been announced ahea
 d of Frameline's 50th festival\, so this is the next round.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Frameline\nLocation: Administered from San Francisco\, United States. O
 pen to filmmakers of all nationalities.\nAward: Grants of up to USD 5\,000
 \, with a standard range of USD 1\,000 to 5\,000\; the jury can recommend 
 amounts above or below that range. No application fee.\nDuration: Submissi
 on window opens 31 August 2026 and closes 9 October 2026\, with notificati
 on in January 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.frameline.org/artist-development/
 completion-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.frameline.org/artist-development/completion-fund?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Administered from San Francisco\, United States. Open to filmmaker
 s of all nationalities.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
